# agentboard runtime scratch
# `.agentboard/` itself is tracked - it IS the board, and a clone that arrived
# without it cannot tell who holds which file. Only the two per-machine
# artefacts are ignored: the advisory flock and the scratch of an interrupted
# save.
# `init` now seeds these same two rules inside every store it writes, so a board
# dropped into a foreign repo keeps itself clean without editing that repo's
# root file. These lines are the second brace: they cover stores created before
# that rule existed, and they are what
# TestQuietWrites::test_the_lock_and_the_scratch_are_the_two_ignored_names
# pins, so widening either list back to `.agentboard*` fails a test rather than
# silently untracking the board.
**/.agentboard/.lock
**/.agentboard/.tmp-*.yaml
**/.agentboard/**/*.tmp-*.yaml

